## Context
Tracker 1052 retired the model-level x effort chooser; the orchestrator now
chooses workers from the `skills/route` grid and states why. A first review
round ran right after (2026-10-09): contradiction, prompt-level and efficiency
seats, a cross-family Luna seat, and an Opus review of the mechanical test
suite; their fixes landed in #1283, #1286 to #1289. That round read a harness
that had not yet been used under the new rules. This ticket asks for a second
round once the new mechanisms have run for real.

## Scope
Blocked by 1072: this is the global coherence review, so it starts from the
harness as left by the per-diff fixes of 1072, not before.
Run after several real `/gaze` and `/raid` runs have used the new launch line,
the review-pr manifest check (`scripts/panel-manifest-check.py`) and the
risk-scaled decorrelation doctrine, so the review can read behaviour, not only
text.
- Contradiction seat plus one other-family seat over AGENTS.md, rules/, skills/,
  agents/, profiles/, adapters/ (non-contradiction of who chooses, who reviews,
  how to pin).
- Prompt-level seat over the routing material and the resident rules: right
  level for a capable model, no restated defaults, no incident history.
- Efficiency seat: resident-context bytes before and after #1286, cost per full
  `/gaze` under the new seat table with prices taken from grid.json, and
  whether the launch line is actually written in recent sessions (read the
  traces, do not guess).
- Mechanical suite (Opus): padme, doudou and a secretless box (env -i, no CLIs,
  no network). Include the uv path now (`uv sync --frozen` in CI and locally),
  the guarded rtk hook, the xdist fallback, and the exit-77 skip mapping.
  Positive control for every null result.
- Check the open gaps recorded after the first round: Pi `reviewer`,
  `code-reviewer` and `planner` agents never run; Codex `fork_turns` "all" not
  tested; the adherence criterion of ticket 1070 was met only as a rule-text
  check; the two unexplained CI flakes (cross-PR collision suite, temp-repo git
  exit 128) now print their output on failure, so read any new occurrence.
- Trace ingestion: check that the trace scripts (`scripts/trace-stats.py` and
  siblings) attribute worktree-named session folders under `~/.claude/projects`
  to their project, and whether any reads the Codex seats' transcripts in
  `~/.codex/sessions/`; positive control on a known 1072 session.
- Memory: the notes on Claude Code subagent mechanics still mention tier pins
  (left to dream). Confirm dream has refreshed them.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] Each seat reports findings with `path:line` anchors; every finding is
      fixed, ticketed above the severity floor, or recorded as accepted
- [ ] At least one seat is from another model family than the coordinator
- [ ] Resident-context byte counts reported before and after
- [ ] The suite result is reported for padme, doudou and the secretless run
- [ ] `make check` passes after the fixes
